@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il34-nouns`

-- National Insurance Law s 342(e) (the Minister's power over an employee of several employers) and the National
-- Insurance (Payment and Deduction of Insurance Contributions from the Pay of an Insured Person Working for Different
-- Employers) Regulations, 5757-1997, which exercise it. Row IL-34, priorities 2 and 3.
-- `src:N` is line N of the Law's deposited text; `ext:[reg-several] N` is line N of the Regulations'
-- (../../registers/source-bundle/regulations/national-insurance-payment-and-deduction-from-employee-of-several-employers-regulations-5757-1997.he.wiki.txt,
-- sha256 per ../../registers/source-bundle/regulations/SOURCES.json, Wikisource consolidation of 2025-05-13).
--
-- HOW THIS FEEDS ROW IL-05. Row IL-05 encodes s 342(d): the "coordinated contributions" and the employee's duty to pay
-- the difference or right to a refund. It declines a deduction that these regulations govern. This module takes the
-- coordinated contributions, the full rate and the sums the employers deducted as INPUTS (IL-05 computes the first two from
-- Schedule J; "the full rate" is the rate on the part of the wage above the reduced collection threshold) and encodes what
-- the regulations add: which employer deducts at the full rate (reg 2), the collection clerk's certificate (reg 3), the
-- secondary employer's permitted deduction and its months (reg 3A, 3B), the duty of forms and accounts (regs 2A, 4), the
-- employee's payment and refund (regs 5, 6) and the linkage of a refund (reg 7).
--
-- THE REGULATIONS' OWN WORDS "HALF THE AVERAGE WAGE" (regs 1 and 2). They are the threshold the Law then called "half the
-- average wage"; the Law now says "the reduced collection threshold" (s 334(a)). The regulations' amounts do not turn on
-- which: reg 2 puts the full rate on the WHOLE wage, and the full rate is the rate of the band above the threshold, wherever the
-- threshold is. So no reading of the threshold gates an answer here (NOTES.md, section "Not gating").
--
-- NEEDS A SOURCE (taken as inputs by name): the National Insurance (Classification of Insured Persons and Determination of
-- Employers) Order 5732-1972 s 2 (who is a "recognised employer"); the Income Tax (Deduction from Salary and Wages and Payment
-- of Employers' Tax) Regulations 5753-1993 reg 5(a) and (e)(1); the National Insurance (Collection of Insurance Contributions)
-- Regulations 5714-1954 reg 2(2) (the payment dates reg 5 names).

§ `The several-employers regulations of 5757-1997`

§§ `Regulation 8: from when regulations 2 and 3 apply`

-- ext:[reg-several] 62 | סעיף 8 – תחולה
-- ext:[reg-several] 63 | תקנות 2 ו־3 יחולו על הכנסתו החודשית של עובד המשתלמת בעד יום כ״ב באדר א׳ התשנ״ז (1 במרס 1997) ואילך.

@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 8 (reg line 63)
GIVETH A DATE
`Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 8 — the day from which regulations 2 and 3 apply` MEANS
    YMD 1997 3 1

@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 8 (reg line 63)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 8 — regulations 2 and 3 apply to a monthly income paid for the day` d MEANS
    Day d AT LEAST Day (`Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 8 — the day from which regulations 2 and 3 apply`)

§§ `Regulation 9: the transition`

-- ext:[reg-several] 65 | סעיף 9 – הוראת מעבר
-- ext:[reg-several] 66 | על אף האמור בתקנה 8, ינכה מעביד את סכום דמי הביטוח לפי תקנות 2 ו־3, לפי הענין, משכר העובד בעד החודשים מרס עד יוני של שנת 1997, מהשכר שהוא משלם לעובד בעד כל אחד מהחודשים יולי עד נובמבר של שנת 1997, בחלקים שווים.

-- The sums due under regs 2 and 3 for March to June 1997 are deducted from the wage paid for each of July to November 1997, in
-- equal parts: five parts.
@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 9 (reg line 66)
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 9 — the month is one of the five months of the transition` `the year` `,` `the month` MEANS
    `the year` EQUALS 1997 AND `the month` AT LEAST 7 AND `the month` AT MOST 11

@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 9 (reg line 66)
GIVEN `the sums due for March to June 1997` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 9 — the equal part deducted in each of the five months` `the sums due for March to June 1997` MEANS
    `the sums due for March to June 1997` DIVIDED BY 5

§§ `Regulation 1: the definitions, as inputs`

-- ext:[reg-several] 14 | סעיף 1 – הגדרות [תיקון: תשנ״ז]
-- ext:[reg-several] 15 | בתקנות אלה –
-- ext:[reg-several] 16 | ”דמי ביטוח מתואמים“ – כמשמעותם בסעיף 342(ד)(1) לחוק;
-- ext:[reg-several] 17 | ”הכנסה כוללת“ – הכנסתו החודשית הכוללת של עובד, מכל מעבידיו;
-- ext:[reg-several] 18 | ”שיעור מלא“ – שיעור הניכוי משכר העובד הקבוע בטור ה׳ בלוח י׳ לחוק, על חלק השכר העולה על מחצית השכר הממוצע;
-- ext:[reg-several] 19 | ”תקנות הניכוי“ – תקנות מס הכנסה ומס מעסיקים (ניכוי ממשכורת ומשכר עבודה ותשלום מס מעסיקים), התשנ״ג–1993;
-- ext:[reg-several] 20 | ”תקנות הגביה“ – תקנות הביטוח הלאומי (גביית דמי ביטוח), התשי״ד–1954.

-- "Full rate" is the rate fixed in column E of Schedule J for the deduction from an employee's wage on the part of the wage above
-- half the average wage. Schedule J's deduction rates are column D in row IL-04 and IL-05 (their fork F22 on s 342(e)(3), which
-- also says column E); the caller supplies the rate, so this module takes no side. "Total income" is the employee's total monthly
-- income from all his employers.

§§ `Regulation 2: who deducts at the full rate, and how much`

-- ext:[reg-several] 22 | סעיף 2 – ניכוי דמי ביטוח משכר [תיקון: תשנ״ח, תשנ״ט]
-- ext:[reg-several] 23 | מעביד כמשמעותו לפי סעיף 2 לצו הביטוח הלאומי (סיווג מבוטחים וקביעת מעבידים), התשל״ב–1972 (להלן – מעביד מוכר) וכן מעביד שתקנה 5(א) או (ה)(1) לתקנות הניכוי חלות לגביו, ינכה דמי ביטוח בשיעור מלא גם מחלק השכר של העובד, שאינו עולה על מחצית השכר הממוצע, כאמור בסעיף 342(ה)(3) לחוק.
-- src:3666 | (ה) השר רשאי לקבוע תנאים, כללים ומועדים בדבר –
-- src:3667 | (1) חובת עובד לדווח למעבידו ולמוסד על היותו עובד אצל מעביד נוסף;
-- src:3668 | (2) תשלום או החזר של ההפרש שבין סכום הניכוי בפועל, לבין סכום דמי הביטוח המתואמים;
-- src:3669 | (3) חובת מעביד לנכות דמי ביטוח בשיעור החל, לפי טור ה׳ בלוח י׳, על הכנסת עובד העולה על מדרגת הגבייה המופחתת, גם מהכנסת העובד שאינה עולה על מדרגת הגבייה המופחתת, אם העובד מועסק אצל מעביד נוסף;
-- src:3670 | (4) אישור המוסד בדבר ניכוי דמי ביטוח בשיעורים הנקובים בטור ה׳ בלוח י׳, לפי הענין, בשונה מההוראות שנקבעו לפי פסקה (3), וכן בדבר חובת מעביד לנכות מהכנסת עובד המועסק על ידי מעבידים שונים, דמי ביטוח בהתאם לאישור המוסד.
-- src:3671 | [note: פורסמו תקנות הביטוח הלאומי (תשלום וניכוי דמי ביטוח משכר מבוטח העובד אצל מעבידים שונים), התשנ״ז–1997.]

-- Reg 2 reaches two kinds of employer: a "recognised employer" under the 1972 Order, and an employer to whom reg 5(a) or (e)(1)
-- of the Income Tax Deduction Regulations applies. Neither text is deposited; both are facts about the employer.
@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 2 (reg line 23)
GIVEN `is a recognised employer under the 1972 Order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 5(a) or (e)(1) of the Income Tax Deduction Regulations applies to him` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 2 — the regulation reaches an employer:` `is a recognised employer under the 1972 Order` `, or one to whom` `reg 5(a) or (e)(1) of the Income Tax Deduction Regulations applies to him` MEANS
    `is a recognised employer under the 1972 Order` OR `reg 5(a) or (e)(1) of the Income Tax Deduction Regulations applies to him`

@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 2 (reg line 23); s 342(c) (source line 3661), row IL-05
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`regulation 2 does not reach this employer, whose deduction is section 342(c)'s (row IL-05)` MEANS
    REFUSE "regulation 2 does not reach this employer, whose deduction is section 342(c)'s (row IL-05)"

-- The employer deducts "also from the part of the wage not exceeding half the average wage": at the full rate, on the whole wage.
@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 2 (reg line 23)
GIVEN `the employer is reached by reg 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the wage` IS A NUMBER
      `the full rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 2 — where` `the employer is reached by reg 2` `, the deduction from a wage of` `the wage` `at the full rate` `the full rate` MEANS
    IF `the employer is reached by reg 2`
    THEN `the wage` TIMES `the full rate`
    ELSE `regulation 2 does not reach this employer, whose deduction is section 342(c)'s (row IL-05)`

§§ `Regulation 2A: the form a recognised employer's employee fills in`

-- ext:[reg-several] 25 | סעיף 2א – עובד אצל מעביד מוכר [תיקון: תשנ״ט]
-- ext:[reg-several] 26 | עובד המועסק על ידי מעביד מוכר חייב למלא בטופס שקבע המוסד פרטים על עבודתו אצל כל מעבידיו ולמסרו למעבידו לפני המועד שבו קיבל את שכרו ובתחילת כל שנת מס.

@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 2A (reg line 26)
GIVEN `the employer is a recognised employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 2A — the employee is bound to fill in the Institute's form` `the employer is a recognised employer` MEANS
    `the employer is a recognised employer`

-- "and hand it to his employer before the day on which he received his wage, and at the start of each tax year". The first limb
-- is a day; the second names no day, so it is a fact the caller reports.
@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 2A (reg line 26)
GIVEN `the day he handed it over` IS A DATE
      `the day he received his wage` IS A DATE
      `he handed it over at the start of the tax year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 2A — the form was handed over in time:` `the day he handed it over` `, the wage received on` `the day he received his wage` `, at the start of the tax year being` `he handed it over at the start of the tax year` MEANS
        Day `the day he handed it over` LESS THAN Day `the day he received his wage`
    AND `he handed it over at the start of the tax year`

§§ `Regulation 3: the collection clerk's certificate`

-- ext:[reg-several] 28 | סעיף 3 – ניכוי דמי ביטוח לפי הוראת פקיד גביה
-- ext:[reg-several] 29 | (א) הוכיח מבוטח העובד אצל מעבידים שונים, להנחת דעתו של פקיד גביה, כי אילו נוכו מהכנסתו הכוללת דמי ביטוח לפי האמור בתקנה 2, היה סכום הניכוי האמור עולה על סכום דמי הביטוח המתואמים, רשאי פקיד הגביה ליתן לעובד אישור המורה למעביד מסוים כי ינכה משכר העובד שיעור שונה של דמי ביטוח לתקופה שיורה, והכל כפי שיקבע פקיד הגביה בהתאם לאומדן דמי הביטוח המתואמים שהעובד חייב בתשלומם.
-- ext:[reg-several] 30 | (ב) הורה פקיד גביה כאמור בתקנת משנה (א), ינכה המעביד דמי ביטוח בהתאם להוראותיו.

-- The clerk may direct an employer to deduct a different rate for a period if the employee proves, to the clerk's satisfaction,
-- that deductions under reg 2 from his total income would exceed the coordinated contributions.
@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3(a) (reg line 29)
GIVEN `the total income` IS A NUMBER
      `the full rate` IS A NUMBER
      `the coordinated contributions` IS A NUMBER
      `he proved it to the clerk's satisfaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3(a) — the clerk may give the employee a certificate: total income` `the total income` `, full rate` `the full rate` `, coordinated contributions` `the coordinated contributions` `, proved to the clerk's satisfaction being` `he proved it to the clerk's satisfaction` MEANS
        `he proved it to the clerk's satisfaction`
    AND `the total income` TIMES `the full rate` GREATER THAN `the coordinated contributions`

§§ `Regulations 3A to 3C: the secondary employer and the refund request`

-- ext:[reg-several] 32 | סעיף 3א – תיאום דמי ביטוח בידי מעסיק [תיקון: תשנ״ח, תשנ״ט]
-- ext:[reg-several] 33 | (א) על אף האמור בתקנה 3, המוסד רשאי להתיר למעביד פלוני (להלן – מעביד משני) שמתקיים בו האמור בתקנה 2, לנכות משכרו של העובד דמי ביטוח בסכום השווה להפרש שבין דמי הביטוח המתואמים לבין הסכום הכולל של דמי הביטוח שנוכה בעד אותו חודש, משכרו של העובד המשתלם בידי כל אחד ממעבידיו האחרים.
-- ext:[reg-several] 34 | (ב) הניכוי לפי הוראת תקנת משנה (א), ייעשה לגבי כל אחד מהחודשים ינואר עד יוני שבשנת מס (להלן – החציון הראשון), אם העובד המציא אישור שכר ב־1 בינואר של אותה שנת מס ולגבי החודשים יולי עד דצמבר שבשנת מס (להלן – החציון השני), אם העובד המציא אישור שכר, ב־1 ביולי של אותה שנת מס.
-- ext:[reg-several] 35 | (ג) החל עובד לעבוד אצל מעביד משני בחציון הראשון לאחר ה־1 בינואר, או בחציון השני לאחר ה־1 ביוני, יחולו הוראות תקנת משנה (ב) לגבי כל אחד מהחודשים שבהם עבד באותו חציון, אם הגיש אישור שכר בתחילת החודש שבו התחיל לעבוד כאמור.
-- ext:[reg-several] 36 | (ד) בתקנה זו –
-- ext:[reg-several] 37 | ”אישור שכר“ – אישור מכל אחד ממעבידיו של עובד, למעט המעביד המשני, ובו פירוט השכר ששולם לעובד בחודש שקדם בתכוף למועד המצאתו שנקבע בתקנת משנה (ב), לפי הענין, וכן שיעור דמי הביטוח שנוכה מהשכר האמור.
-- ext:[reg-several] 38 | ”מעביד“ – לרבות מעביד מוכר.
-- ext:[reg-several] 40 | סעיף 3ב – עובד אצל מעביד מוכר [תיקון: תשנ״ח, תשנ״ט]
-- ext:[reg-several] 41 | תקנה 3א תחול לגבי עובד המועסק על ידי מעביד מוכר אם המציא העובד למעבידו כאמור פרטים על הכנסותיו.
-- ext:[reg-several] 43 | סעיף 3ג – בקשה להחזר דמי ביטוח ששולמו ביתר [תיקון: תשנ״ח, תשנ״ט]
-- ext:[reg-several] 44 | מבוטח העובד אצל מעבידים שונים שנוכו משכרו דמי ביטוח בסכום העולה על דמי הביטוח המתואמים, יגיש למוסד בקשה להחזר דמי הביטוח, בטופס שקבע המוסד, בצירוף אישור מכל אחד ממעבידיו של העובד, הכולל פרטים על שכרו החודשי, התקופה שבעדה שולם השכר וסכומי דמי הביטוח שנוכו ממנו.

-- 3A(a): the secondary employer deducts the difference between the coordinated contributions and what the employee's other
-- employers deducted for that month. Fork N1 is the case where the others deducted MORE.
@ref NOTES.md fork N1
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`regulation 3A(a) does not say what the secondary employer deducts when the other employers have already deducted more than the coordinated contributions` MEANS
    REFUSE "regulation 3A(a) does not say what the secondary employer deducts when the other employers have already deducted more than the coordinated contributions"

@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(a) (reg line 33); NOTES.md fork N1
GIVEN `the coordinated contributions` IS A NUMBER
      `the total the employee's other employers deducted for the month` IS A NUMBER
      r IS A `A reading of a negative difference under regulation 3A(a)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(a) — the sum the secondary employer may be allowed to deduct: coordinated contributions` `the coordinated contributions` `, the others having deducted` `the total the employee's other employers deducted for the month` `, reading a negative difference as` r MEANS
    IF `the coordinated contributions` AT LEAST `the total the employee's other employers deducted for the month`
    THEN `the coordinated contributions` MINUS `the total the employee's other employers deducted for the month`
    ELSE
        CONSIDER r
        WHEN `a negative difference leaves nothing for the secondary employer to deduct` THEN 0
        WHEN `a negative difference is declined`                                         THEN `regulation 3A(a) does not say what the secondary employer deducts when the other employers have already deducted more than the coordinated contributions`

@ref NOTES.md fork N1 (SHRUG, Meng 2026-10-08)
GIVETH A `A reading of a negative difference under regulation 3A(a)`
`Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(a) — the reading this row takes of a negative difference` MEANS `a negative difference is declined`

@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(a) (reg line 33)
GIVEN `the coordinated contributions` IS A NUMBER
      `the total the employee's other employers deducted for the month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(a) — the sum the secondary employer may be allowed to deduct: coordinated contributions` `the coordinated contributions` `, the others having deducted` `the total the employee's other employers deducted for the month` MEANS
    `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(a) — the sum the secondary employer may be allowed to deduct: coordinated contributions` `the coordinated contributions` `, the others having deducted` `the total the employee's other employers deducted for the month` `, reading a negative difference as` (`Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(a) — the reading this row takes of a negative difference`)

-- 3A(d): a wage certificate is one from each of the other employers, detailing the wage of the month before it is delivered and
-- the rate deducted.
@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(d) (reg line 37)
GIVEN c IS A `A wage certificate under regulation 3A`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(d) — it is a wage certificate` c MEANS
        c's `it is from each of the employee's other employers`
    AND c's `it details the wage paid in the month before the day it was delivered`
    AND c's `it states the rate of contributions deducted`

-- The first day of the half of a tax year that holds a month, and the day the half's certificate is due.
@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b) (reg line 34)
GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the wage certificate of the half of the year holding month` `the month` `of` `the tax year` `is due under reg 3A(b)` MEANS
    IF `the month` AT MOST 6 THEN YMD `the tax year` 1 1 ELSE YMD `the tax year` 7 1

-- 3A(b): the deduction is made for each of January to June if the employee delivered a wage certificate on 1 January of the tax year,
-- and for each of July to December if he delivered one on 1 July.
-- 3A(c): if he began with the secondary employer in the first half after 1 January, or in the second half after 1 June, (b) applies
-- to each month he worked in that half, if he delivered the certificate at the beginning of the month in which he began.
-- ("after 1 June" in the second half is every day of it; the first half's reference is 1 January. NOTES.md section "Oddities".)
@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b) and (c) (reg lines 34-35)
GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
      c IS A `A wage certificate under regulation 3A`
      `the day he began with the secondary employer` IS A DATE
      `he worked for the secondary employer in the month` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b)-(c) — the secondary employer may deduct for month` `the month` `of` `the tax year` `, the certificate being` c `, he having begun on` `the day he began with the secondary employer` `and worked in the month being` `he worked for the secondary employer in the month` MEANS
    IF `the month` LESS THAN 1 OR `the month` GREATER THAN 12
    THEN `a month of the tax year is numbered from 1 to 12`
    ELSE
            `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(d) — it is a wage certificate` c
        AND `he worked for the secondary employer in the month`
        AND (`by 3A(b)` OR `by 3A(c)`)
    WHERE
        `the first half` MEANS `the month` AT MOST 6
        `by 3A(b)` MEANS Day (c's `the day it was delivered`) EQUALS Day (`the day the wage certificate of the half of the year holding month` `the month` `of` `the tax year` `is due under reg 3A(b)`)
        `the half began` MEANS `the day the wage certificate of the half of the year holding month` `the month` `of` `the tax year` `is due under reg 3A(b)`
        `the day he began is in this half` MEANS
                DATE_YEAR `the day he began with the secondary employer` EQUALS `the tax year`
            AND (DATE_MONTH `the day he began with the secondary employer` AT MOST 6) EQUALS `the first half`
        `he began after the reference day of the half` MEANS
            IF `the first half`
            THEN Day `the day he began with the secondary employer` GREATER THAN Day (YMD `the tax year` 1 1)
            ELSE Day `the day he began with the secondary employer` GREATER THAN Day (YMD `the tax year` 6 1)
        `by 3A(c)` MEANS
                `the day he began is in this half`
            AND `he began after the reference day of the half`
            AND Day (c's `the day it was delivered`) EQUALS Day (YMD `the tax year` (DATE_MONTH `the day he began with the secondary employer`) 1)
            AND `the month` AT LEAST (DATE_MONTH `the day he began with the secondary employer`)

@ref Schedule K, "רבעון" (source line 4771)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`a month of the tax year is numbered from 1 to 12` MEANS
    REFUSE "a month of the tax year is numbered from 1 to 12"

-- 3B: reg 3A reaches an employee of a recognised employer if he gave his employer details of his incomes under reg 2A. For an
-- employer reached by reg 2 on the other limb (the Income Tax Deduction Regulations), 3A(a) applies by its own terms.
@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3B (reg line 41), reg 3A(a) (reg line 33)
GIVEN `the employer is reached by reg 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer is a recognised employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee gave his employer details of his incomes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3B — reg 3A applies: employer reached by reg 2 being` `the employer is reached by reg 2` `, recognised being` `the employer is a recognised employer` `, details given being` `the employee gave his employer details of his incomes` MEANS
        `the employer is reached by reg 2`
    AND ((NOT `the employer is a recognised employer`) OR `the employee gave his employer details of his incomes`)

-- 3C: an employee from whose wage more than the coordinated contributions were deducted asks the Institute for a refund on its form,
-- with a certificate from each employer.
@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3C (reg line 44)
GIVEN `the sum deducted` IS A NUMBER
      `the coordinated contributions` IS A NUMBER
      q IS A `A refund request under regulation 3C`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3C — a complete request for a refund: deducted` `the sum deducted` `, coordinated contributions` `the coordinated contributions` `, request` q MEANS
        `the sum deducted` GREATER THAN `the coordinated contributions`
    AND q's `it is on the Institute's form`
    AND q's `it has a certificate from each of the employee's employers`
    AND q's `each certificate gives the monthly wage, the period of the wage and the sums deducted`

§§ `Regulation 4: the account`

-- ext:[reg-several] 46 | סעיף 4 – דין וחשבון [תיקון: תשנ״ח, תשנ״ט]
-- ext:[reg-several] 47 | (א) עובד שהכנסתו הכוללת בחודש פלוני בשנת מס עלתה על ההכנסה המרבית הקבועה בפרט 1 שבלוח י״א לחוק (להלן – שנת הדיווח), אשר ניתן לו אישור מפקיד גביה כאמור בתקנה 3, או שמעבידו ניכה משכרו דמי ביטוח בהתאם לתקנה 3א, יגיש למוסד עד 31 ביולי של שנת המס שלאחריה, דין וחשבון על הכנסותיו בשנת הדיווח ועל סכומי דמי הביטוח שנוכו מהכנסותיו כאמור.
-- ext:[reg-several] 48 | (ב) מעביד ימסור לעובדו החייב להגיש דין וחשבון לפי תקנת משנה (א), או המגיש בקשה לפי תקנה 3ב [note: [צ״ל: 3ג]], בתום שנת הדיווח או בתום התקופה שלגביה מבקש העובד להגיש בקשה לפי תקנה 3ב [note: [צ״ל: 3ג]], לפי הענין, אישור הכולל פרטים על שכרו החודשי בשנה או בתקופה האמורה, וסכומי דמי הביטוח שנוכו ממנו.

-- (a): an employee whose total income in some month of a tax year exceeded the maximum income of Schedule K item 1, and who was given
-- a certificate by a collection clerk under reg 3 or whose employer deducted under reg 3A, files an account of that year's incomes
-- and deductions by 31 July of the next tax year. The maximum income is an input (row IL-05's Schedule K module holds it).
@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 4(a) (reg line 47)
GIVEN `the highest total income in a month of the tax year` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum income of Schedule K item 1` IS A NUMBER
      `a collection clerk gave him a certificate under reg 3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `his employer deducted under reg 3A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 4(a) — the employee must file an account: highest monthly income` `the highest total income in a month of the tax year` `, maximum income` `the maximum income of Schedule K item 1` `, certificate under reg 3 being` `a collection clerk gave him a certificate under reg 3` `, deduction under reg 3A being` `his employer deducted under reg 3A` MEANS
        `the highest total income in a month of the tax year` GREATER THAN `the maximum income of Schedule K item 1`
    AND (`a collection clerk gave him a certificate under reg 3` OR `his employer deducted under reg 3A`)

@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 4(a) (reg line 47)
GIVEN `the reporting year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 4(a) — the day by which the account is due, for the tax year` `the reporting year` MEANS
    YMD (`the reporting year` PLUS 1) 7 31

§§ `Regulation 5: the employee pays the difference`

-- ext:[reg-several] 50 | סעיף 5 – תשלום דמי ביטוח בידי העובד
-- ext:[reg-several] 51 | מבוטח העובד אצל מעבידים שונים החייב בתשלום דמי ביטוח בסכום ההפרש שבין סכום דמי הביטוח המתואמים לבין סכום הניכוי בפועל כמשמעותו בסעיף 342(ד)(1) לחוק, ישלמם במועדי תשלום דמי הביטוח האמורים בתקנה 2(2) לתקנות הגביה.

-- The employee pays the difference between the coordinated contributions and the actual deduction (s 342(d)(1)), at the payment
-- dates of reg 2(2) of the Collection Regulations (not deposited): the dates are the caller's.
@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 5 (reg line 51); s 342(d)(1) (source line 3664)
GIVEN `the coordinated contributions` IS A NUMBER
      `the actual deduction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 5 — the difference the employee pays: coordinated contributions` `the coordinated contributions` `, actual deduction` `the actual deduction` MEANS
    max 0 (`the coordinated contributions` MINUS `the actual deduction`)

§§ `Regulation 6: the refund`

-- ext:[reg-several] 53 | סעיף 6 – החזר דמי ביטוח לעובד [תיקון: תשנ״ח, תשנ״ט]
-- ext:[reg-several] 54 | (א) מבוטח העובד אצל מעבידים שונים שהגיש למוסד דין וחשבון לפי תקנה 4 או בקשה להחזר דמי ביטוח לפי סעיף 3ב [note: [צ״ל: תקנה 3ג]], יחזיר לו המוסד כל סכום שנוכה משכרו החודשי העולה על סכום דמי הביטוח המתואמים בעד אותו חודש, ובלבד שהדין וחשבון הוגש למוסד בתוך שבע שנים מסוף שנת המס שבה נוכה הסכום האמור.
-- ext:[reg-several] 55 | (ב) סכום ההחזר האמור בתקנת משנה (א), יוחזר למבוטח בתוך שלושה חודשים מיום קבלת הבקשה במוסד ובלבד שאם יש למוסד ספק בדבר זכותו של המבוטח להחזר הסכום, כולו או חלקו, רשאי המוסד להשהות את ההחזר עד לבירור הספק, ויודיע על כך למבוטח.

@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 6(a) (reg line 54)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`regulation 6(a) refunds on an account filed within seven years of the end of the tax year and does not say what follows a later account` MEANS
    REFUSE "regulation 6(a) refunds on an account filed within seven years of the end of the tax year and does not say what follows a later account"

-- "provided that the account was filed with the Institute within seven years of the end of the tax year in which the sum was
-- deducted": the end of the tax year is 31 December; seven years on is 31 December seven years later, the last day to file.
@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 6(a) (reg line 54)
GIVEN `the tax year of the deduction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 6(a) — the last day to file the account for the tax year` `the tax year of the deduction` MEANS
    YMD (`the tax year of the deduction` PLUS 7) 12 31

@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 6(a) (reg line 54)
GIVEN `the tax year of the deduction` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the account was filed` IS A DATE
      `the sum deducted from the month's wage` IS A NUMBER
      `the coordinated contributions for the month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 6(a) — the refund for a month of the tax year` `the tax year of the deduction` `, the account filed on` `the day the account was filed` `, deducted` `the sum deducted from the month's wage` `, coordinated contributions` `the coordinated contributions for the month` MEANS
    IF Day `the day the account was filed` AT MOST Day (`Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 6(a) — the last day to file the account for the tax year` `the tax year of the deduction`)
    THEN max 0 (`the sum deducted from the month's wage` MINUS `the coordinated contributions for the month`)
    ELSE `regulation 6(a) refunds on an account filed within seven years of the end of the tax year and does not say what follows a later account`

@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 6(b) (reg line 55)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`regulation 6(b) lets the Institute delay the refund until its doubt is cleared, so no day is due` MEANS
    REFUSE "regulation 6(b) lets the Institute delay the refund until its doubt is cleared, so no day is due"

-- (b): the refund is returned within three months of the day the request reached the Institute, unless the Institute doubts the right
-- (all or part), in which case it may delay it until the doubt is cleared and tells the insured.
@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 6(b) (reg line 55)
GIVEN `the day the request reached the Institute` IS A DATE
      `the Institute doubts the right to the refund` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 6(b) — the day by which the refund is due: request received` `the day the request reached the Institute` `, doubt being` `the Institute doubts the right to the refund` MEANS
    IF `the Institute doubts the right to the refund`
    THEN `regulation 6(b) lets the Institute delay the refund until its doubt is cleared, so no day is due`
    ELSE `add months` `the day the request reached the Institute` 3

§§ `Regulation 7: linkage`

-- ext:[reg-several] 57 | סעיף 7 – הצמדה [תיקון: תשנ״ח]
-- ext:[reg-several] 58 | על החזר לפי תקנה 6 יחולו הוראות סעיף 362 לחוק בשינויים המחויבים, ולענין זה –
-- ext:[reg-several] 59 | (1) לגבי החזר המתייחס לחודש מסוים בשנת מס – יראו את היום שבו שולם תשלום היתר, כמועד התשלום החל לגבי עובד לפי סעיף 353 לחוק;
-- ext:[reg-several] 60 | (2) לגבי החזר המתייחס לשנת מס – תחושב התוספת שלפי סעיף 362 לחוק, לפי שיעור עליית המדד שפורסם לאחרונה לפני יום תשלום ההחזר, לעומת המדד שפורסם לאחרונה לפני המועד שנקבע לתשלום דמי הביטוח בסעיף 353(א) לחוק.

-- (1): for a refund relating to a month of a tax year the day the excess was paid is taken as the payment date for an employee under
-- s 353: the 15th of the month after the payment period (s 353(a)). Section 353(b) moves that day when it follows rest days; the
-- calendar of rest days is not in the sources, so the day below is the day BEFORE any such move.
@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 7(1) (reg line 59); s 353(a) (National Insurance Law source line 3846)
GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 7(1) — the day the excess is taken to have been paid, before any move under s 353(b), for month` `the month` `of` `the tax year` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the month` LESS THAN 1 OR `the month` GREATER THAN 12 THEN REFUSE "a month of the tax year is numbered from 1 to 12"
           IF `the month` EQUALS 12                                   THEN YMD (`the tax year` PLUS 1) 1 15
           OTHERWISE                                                       YMD `the tax year` (`the month` PLUS 1) 15

@ref NOTES.md fork N2
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 362(a)(1) adds the rate of rise of the index and says nothing of a fall` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 362(a)(1) adds the rate of rise of the index and says nothing of a fall"

-- (2): for a refund relating to a tax year the addition is the rate of rise of the index last published before the refund day against
-- the index last published before the day s 353(a) fixes for the payment. The two index readings are inputs.
@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 7(2) (reg line 60); NOTES.md fork N2
GIVEN `the refund` IS A NUMBER
      `the index last published before the day s 353(a) fixes for payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the index last published before the refund day` IS A NUMBER
      r IS A `A reading of a fall in the index under regulation 7(2)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 7(2) — the addition to a refund of` `the refund` `, the index being` `the index last published before the day s 353(a) fixes for payment` `then and` `the index last published before the refund day` `at the refund, reading a fall as` r MEANS
    IF `the index last published before the refund day` AT LEAST `the index last published before the day s 353(a) fixes for payment`
    THEN `the refund` TIMES (`the index last published before the refund day` DIVIDED BY `the index last published before the day s 353(a) fixes for payment` MINUS 1)
    ELSE
        CONSIDER r
        WHEN `a fall in the index leaves no addition`                          THEN 0
        WHEN `a fall in the index reduces the refund by the rate of the fall`  THEN `the refund` TIMES (`the index last published before the refund day` DIVIDED BY `the index last published before the day s 353(a) fixes for payment` MINUS 1)
        WHEN `a fall in the index is declined`                                 THEN `section 362(a)(1) adds the rate of rise of the index and says nothing of a fall`

@ref NOTES.md fork N2 (SHRUG, Meng 2026-10-08)
GIVETH A `A reading of a fall in the index under regulation 7(2)`
`Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 7(2) — the reading this row takes of a fall in the index` MEANS `a fall in the index is declined`

@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 7(2) (reg line 60)
GIVEN `the refund` IS A NUMBER
      `the index last published before the day s 353(a) fixes for payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the index last published before the refund day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 7(2) — the addition to a refund of` `the refund` `, the index being` `the index last published before the day s 353(a) fixes for payment` `then and` `the index last published before the refund day` `at the refund` MEANS
    `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 7(2) — the addition to a refund of` `the refund` `, the index being` `the index last published before the day s 353(a) fixes for payment` `then and` `the index last published before the refund day` `at the refund, reading a fall as` (`Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 7(2) — the reading this row takes of a fall in the index`)
